{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BZ6EUNDu2nF47szxRCKYCG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我先检查已有的实验数据和计划，确保预测与已确认结果一致。\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Median 档叙事：SDF 是有效的 geometric safety probe，但 LoRA 本身贡献了非小部分 CAR 提升（~35-40%），\n  SDF 增量约 +12-17pp。Phase 2 λ=0 结果为 informative negative——TSR 恢复但 CAR 回落，证明 safety\n  encoding 不持久，需持续 supervision。OpenVLA 验证 fake safety 存在但信号弱于 Pi0。spatial_bowl\n  SDF 效果存在但弱于 object_pudding。论文定位 diagnostic paper，SDF 作为 probe 而非 solution。\n  Acceptance 估算 50-60%。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"A1 EE displacement re-eval (50 episodes)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      用修复后 eval 脚本重跑 A1 (Pi0+LoRA+SDF) model 在 object_pudding 上 50 episodes，\n      提取真实 EE displacement 以定量确认 Claim 1 fake safety。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes: 50\n      avg_TSR: 0\n      avg_CAR: 91.0\n      avg_ee_displacement_m: 0.0021\n      avg_obstacle_displacement_mm: 0.003\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.995\n      real_safe_count: 0\n      episodes_with_ee_disp_gt_0p1m: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 800ep rerun (eval_a1_lora_object_v11_rerun) 确认 CAR=91.5%、fake_safe_rate=99.6%、\n      obstacle displacement 中位数 ~5nm。在 median 档下，修复后脚本新增的 EE displacement 字段预计\n      同样极低（~2mm），因为 A1 模型 TSR=0% 表明 action collapse——robot 几乎不动，EE 位移自然极小。\n      这 50ep sanity check 应与 800ep 数据高度一致，确认 \"EE displacement 接近零 = fake safety\"\n      的定量证据链。不会出现意外高 EE displacement，因为 action collapse 是结构性的。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"A1 EE Displacement Sanity Check (50ep)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"800ep Rerun\", \"50ep Re-eval\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"TSR\", \"0%\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"CAR\", \"91.5%\", \"~91%\"]\n          - [\"Fake Safe Rate\", \"99.6%\", \"~99.5%\"]\n          - [\"Avg Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"0.003\", \"~0.003\"]\n          - [\"Avg EE Disp (m)\", \"N/A (old script)\", \"~0.002\"]\n          - [\"Episodes EE>0.1m\", \"N/A\", \"0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: per-episode EE displacement 分布, 预期全部集中在 <5mm, 与 800ep obstacle displacement 分布形态一致\"\n    analysis: >\n      确认 A1 的 fake safety 同时表现为 obstacle displacement ≈0 和 EE displacement ≈0。\n      这两个独立指标双重验证 action collapse。50ep 与 800ep 一致则不需要 full re-eval (plan_011 取消)。\n      论文中可同时报告两种 displacement 指标增强 Claim 1 说服力。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA zero-shot SafeLIBERO eval (200 episodes)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      Base OpenVLA-7B 在 object_pudding 4 tasks 零样本 eval，200 episodes，\n      验证 fake safety 或 geometric path safety 在第三 model family 上的表现。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes: 200\n      avg_TSR: 8.0\n      avg_CAR: 72.0\n      avg_obstacle_displacement_mm: 12.0\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.70\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 82\n      task1_TSR: 18\n      task1_CAR: 52\n      task2_TSR: 6\n      task2_CAR: 80\n      task3_TSR: 4\n      task3_CAR: 74\n      ee_displacement_m: 0.08\n      model_families_showing_fake_safety: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：OpenVLA eval 成功但 fake safety 信号弱于 Pi0。OpenVLA-7B 是更小的\n      模型（7B vs Pi0 ~3B action head），zero-shot 在 SafeLIBERO 上 TSR 预计很低（~5-10%），\n      因为它没有在该 benchmark 上微调。低 TSR 意味着大量 episode 中 robot 运动有限但非完全\n      collapse（OpenVLA 的 action space 与 Pi0 不同，倾向于产生小但非零的动作）。因此 CAR 会\n      较高（~72%）但 fake_safe_rate 约 70%——低于 Pi0 的 99.6% 因为 OpenVLA 不会完全 freeze，\n      会有一些小幅运动导致 obstacle displacement 偶尔超过 0.1mm 阈值。这给出 \"fake safety\n      exists in OpenVLA but weaker\" 的 median 结论：第三 model family 确认了现象存在，\n      但强度不一致，需在论文中 qualify。部分 task（如 chocolate_pudding 有更大障碍物）CAR\n      会更低因为 OpenVLA 即使小运动也会碰到。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"OpenVLA Zero-Shot Fake Safety Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Fake Safe Rate\", \"Avg Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"Avg EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0 A1 (LoRA+SDF)\", \"0%\", \"91.5%\", \"99.6%\", \"0.003\", \"~0.002\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 Baseline\", \"73%\", \"28%\", \"98.2% (of safe eps)\", \"150.8\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA-7B Zero-Shot\", \"~8%\", \"~72%\", \"~70%\", \"~12\", \"~0.08\"]\n      - name: \"OpenVLA Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"Notes\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"4%\", \"82%\", \"~5\", \"low motion, mostly fake safe\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"18%\", \"52%\", \"~28\", \"larger obstacle, more real collisions\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"6%\", \"80%\", \"~8\", \"moderate fake safety\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"4%\", \"74%\", \"~10\", \"mixed fake/geometric safety\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: 3 model families on TSR vs CAR plane, 标注 fake_safe_rate 作为 marker size, 展示 cross-model fake safety pattern\"\n      - \"Bar chart: fake_safe_rate comparison across Pi0 A1 / Pi0.5 baseline / OpenVLA, 展示现象普遍性但强度差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA 确认 fake safety 存在于第三 model family，使 Claim 1 从 \"Pi0-specific\" 升级为\n      \"cross-model phenomenon\"。但信号弱于 Pi0（70% vs 99.6%），论文需 qualify：fake safety\n      的严重程度与 model capability 和 action space 结构相关。Pi0 action collapse 最极端，\n      OpenVLA 有部分运动但仍大量 fake safe。Pi0.5 的 fake safe 集中在 safe episodes 中\n      （task capability 高所以 safe episodes 少）。三个 model family 共同支持 \"CAR metric is\n      systematically contaminated\" 但机制略有不同。R1 泛化性 concern 从 \"2 models\" 升级到\n      \"3 models\"，acceptance 估算从 ~40% 提升到 ~55%。可能需要 debug OpenVLA 的 action\n      decoding 确保 eval 正确运行（median 档预期部分 debug 时间）。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds, 30K checkpoint)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      LoRA baseline (Pi0.5 + LoRA, 无 SDF) 训练完成后在 object_pudding 200ep eval，\n      2 seeds 取均值，确定 LoRA-only CAR 从而决定 SDF 归因强度。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_TSR: 38.0\n      seed0_CAR: 37.0\n      seed0_ee_disp: 0.32\n      seed0_fake_safe_rate: 0.15\n      seed1_TSR: 35.0\n      seed1_CAR: 39.0\n      seed1_ee_disp: 0.29\n      seed1_fake_safe_rate: 0.18\n      avg_TSR: 36.5\n      avg_CAR: 38.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.305\n      avg_fake_safe_rate: 0.165\n      sdf_delta_CAR: 14.5\n      n_episodes_per_seed: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设 LoRA-only CAR 在 35-42% 范围。逻辑：Pi0.5 baseline（无 LoRA 无 SDF）\n      CAR=26.8%。LoRA 微调增加模型在 SafeLIBERO 上的 capacity，但没有 geometric supervision\n      引导避障。LoRA 可能通过学到 task-specific 运动模式间接提升 CAR——比如学会更高效的路径\n      从而减少与障碍物接触的机会。但这不是 intentional avoidance。预计 TSR ~36.5%（低于\n      baseline 73% 因为 LoRA 在 SafeLIBERO 上的 fine-tuning 可能引入 distribution shift，\n      但高于 SDF 版本的 5-9% 因为没有 SDF loss 干扰 task execution）。CAR ~38% 意味着\n      SDF 增量 = 52.5% (avg SDF CAR) - 38% = +14.5pp。这落在 median 档的 10-18pp 范围内。\n      LoRA 本身提供 +11pp over baseline（38% - 27%），SDF 额外提供 +14.5pp。叙事变为\n      \"LoRA helps, SDF adds major benefit\"——第二行归因表。fake_safe_rate 约 16% 因为部分\n      episode 中 LoRA 模型运动受限但非完全 collapse。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"LoRA Attribution Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe Rate\", \"Delta CAR vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 Baseline (no FT)\", \"73%\", \"27%\", \"0.15\", \"98.2%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA only\", \"~36.5%\", \"~38%\", \"~0.31\", \"~16.5%\", \"+11pp\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.005)\", \"5.5-9.5%\", \"50-55%\", \"~0.50\", \"0%\", \"+25pp\"]\n      - name: \"SDF vs LoRA Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Component\", \"CAR Contribution\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline geometric path\", \"27%\", \"Inherent path safety of capable model\"]\n          - [\"LoRA capacity effect\", \"+11pp → 38%\", \"Task-specific motion patterns reduce incidental contact\"]\n          - [\"SDF geometric supervision\", \"+14.5pp → 52.5%\", \"Intentional collision avoidance from SDF gradient\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Lambda-CAR/TSR curve (Fig 5): x=lambda {0(LoRA), 0.005, 0.01}, y1=CAR, y2=TSR, 展示 dose-dependent tradeoff, LoRA baseline 作为 λ=0 anchor point\"\n    analysis: >\n      LoRA-only CAR ~38% 确认 SDF 不是唯一驱动力——LoRA 本身通过 capacity 增加间接提升了\n      CAR。但 SDF 增量 +14.5pp 仍然显著且方向一致（3 seeds 确认）。Claim 4 措辞需调整为\n      \"SDF provides additive safety benefit beyond LoRA capacity — geometric supervision\n      amplifies rather than solely drives collision avoidance.\" Lambda 曲线现在有 3 个点\n      (0/0.005/0.01)，呈现 monotonic CAR 增加 + TSR 下降的 dose-dependent pattern。\n      如果后续有 λ=0.1 数据则曲线更完整。fake_safe_rate 从 baseline 98.2% → LoRA 16.5% →\n      SDF 0% 的递减也是有价值的发现：LoRA 微调本身就大幅减少了 fake safety（因为 TSR 下降\n      意味着 model 不再是 baseline 的 \"高能力低碰撞\" 模式），SDF 则完全消除 fake safety。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline training completion (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      Pi0.5 + LoRA only (无 SDF loss) 训练到 30K steps, 2 seeds。已在运行中。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_steps_completed: 30000\n      seed0_best_loss: 0.0068\n      seed0_final_loss: 0.0085\n      seed1_steps_completed: 30000\n      seed1_best_loss: 0.0072\n      seed1_final_loss: 0.0090\n      wall_time_hours_per_seed: 16\n    result_rationale: >\n      LoRA-only 训练 loss 预计低于 A1 (LoRA+SDF) 因为没有 SDF auxiliary loss 的干扰。\n      已有 A1 数据：s0_l005 best_loss=0.00786, s1_l005 best_loss=0.01143, s2_l005 \n      best_loss=0.00874。LoRA-only 去掉 SDF loss 后 action loss 应更低（best ~0.007），\n      因为全部 gradient capacity 用于 action prediction。训练应正常完成，无 collapse 风险\n      （LoRA-only 是标准 fine-tuning，比 SDF auxiliary 训练更稳定）。当前 step 26000/30000,\n      预计 ~3.5h 完成。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练本身是 dependency，关键在 eval 结果。loss 曲线可作为 supplementary 展示\n      SDF loss 对 action loss 的干扰程度。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 λ=0 ablation training (seed2, from 10K SDF checkpoint)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      从 Pi0.5+A1 s2 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume 训练 with λ=0 (关闭 SDF loss)，\n      训练到 30K，验证 safety encoding 是否在去除 SDF 后保留。\n    expected_results:\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      best_action_loss: 0.0075\n      final_action_loss: 0.0092\n      training_stable: true\n      wall_time_hours: 16\n      sdf_loss_at_resume: 0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 SDF-trained checkpoint resume with λ=0 时，action loss 预计初始偏高（因为 SDF\n      训练 10K 步偏离了 pure action prediction 的 optimum），然后逐步恢复。训练本身应该\n      稳定——只是标准 LoRA fine-tuning 从一个非标准初始化点开始。最终 action loss 应\n      接近 LoRA-only 水平（~0.008）但可能略高因为 10K 步的 SDF 训练改变了 representation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练结果本身不直接回答科学问题——关键是 eval (plan_006)。但 loss 曲线可以展示\n      action loss 从 SDF-perturbed state 恢复的动态，作为 \"safety encoding 被覆盖\" \n      的间接证据。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 λ=0 eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Phase 2 训练完成后 eval (200 episodes)，提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement，\n      判断 safety encoding 是否保留。\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 42.0\n      avg_CAR: 32.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.28\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.12\n      task0_TSR: 30\n      task0_CAR: 38\n      task1_TSR: 68\n      task1_CAR: 26\n      task2_TSR: 20\n      task2_CAR: 52\n      task3_TSR: 50\n      task3_CAR: 12\n      n_episodes: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设：TSR 恢复到 30-50% 但 CAR 回落至 30-35%。逻辑链：(1) 关闭 SDF loss\n      后模型恢复 task execution 能力（TSR 从 5-9% 回到 ~42%，不完全恢复到 baseline 73%\n      因为 10K 步 SDF 训练改变了 representation 且只有 20K 步恢复时间）；(2) CAR 回落到 ~32%\n      接近 LoRA-only 水平（~38%）甚至略低，说明 SDF 诱导的 safety encoding 没有被 \"烙印\"\n      到 representation 中——一旦 loss signal 消失，model 迅速遗忘。这是 informative negative：\n      safety 需要 continuous supervision，10K 步的 geometric training 不足以产生持久的\n      behavioral change。TSR 42% < baseline 73% 说明 SDF 训练 phase 造成了部分不可逆的\n      capability 损失（task performance 未完全恢复），但不是 catastrophic（仍有合理的 task\n      completion）。CAR 32% 接近 baseline 27% + LoRA effect，意味着 SDF 的 safety 增量\n      完全消失。fake_safe_rate ~12% 类似 LoRA-only 水平。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Phase 2 λ=0 Ablation Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 Baseline\", \"73%\", \"27%\", \"0.15\", \"98.2%\"]\n          - [\"SDF λ=0.005 (continuous)\", \"5.5-9.5%\", \"50-55%\", \"0.50\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"Phase 2 λ=0 (from 10K SDF)\", \"~42%\", \"~32%\", \"~0.28\", \"~12%\"]\n          - [\"LoRA only (no SDF ever)\", \"~36.5%\", \"~38%\", \"~0.31\", \"~16.5%\"]\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Interpretation Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Outcome\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Interpretation\", \"Paper Impact\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Observed (median)\", \"42%\", \"32%\", \"Safety encoding not persistent\", \"Informative negative\"]\n          - [\"Upgrade threshold\", \">=40%\", \">=40%\", \"Two-phase strategy works\", \"Solution paper\"]\n          - [\"Strong negative\", \"<20%\", \"any\", \"SDF causes irreversible damage\", \"Supports extreme tradeoff\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training dynamics plot: action loss over steps 10K-30K for Phase 2 vs LoRA-only vs SDF-continuous, showing recovery trajectory\"\n      - \"TSR-CAR scatter: Phase 2 point added to existing scatter, showing it lands between LoRA-only and baseline\"\n    analysis: >\n      Phase 2 结果为 informative negative：TSR 恢复（42%）证明 SDF 训练没有 permanently\n      破坏 task capability，但 CAR 回落到 ~32% 证明 safety encoding 不持久。这排除了\n      \"two-phase training strategy\" 作为 technical contribution（不满足 TSR≥40% + CAR≥40%\n      双门槛）。论文写入方式：\"Removing SDF supervision recovers task performance (TSR: 9%→42%)\n      but safety gains are lost (CAR: 52%→32%), indicating that SDF-induced collision avoidance\n      requires continuous geometric supervision rather than being encoded as a persistent\n      behavioral prior.\" 这支持 diagnostic paper 定位——问题可解但 naive 方法不持久。\n      R3 \"no solution\" concern 通过此 negative result + Phase 2/lambda tuning 作为\n      future work 来应对。CAR 32% 略低于 LoRA-only 38%（差 6pp）可能在 noise 范围内，\n      也可能说明 SDF 训练 phase 对 representation 的 perturbation 稍微损害了 LoRA \n      已学到的 incidental safety patterns。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 训练 (seed0, λ=0.005)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (A1) 在 spatial_bowl scene 训练 30K steps，\n      验证 SDF 效果是否跨 scene 泛化。\n    expected_results:\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      best_loss: 0.0125\n      final_loss: 0.0155\n      wall_time_hours: 34\n      sdf_loss_final: 0.0035\n    result_rationale: >\n      spatial_bowl 是更难的 scene（障碍物布局不同，碰撞部位更多 arm-body 而非 EE）。\n      SDF training loss 预计略高于 object_pudding（s0_l005 best=0.00786）因为 scene\n      complexity 增加了 action prediction 难度。训练本身应正常完成（已确认 A1 训练在\n      object_pudding 上 3 seeds 稳定）。当前 11329/30000 步，~24h 剩余。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练是 dependency，关键在 eval (plan_008)。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval，验证跨场景 CAR/TSR pattern。200 episodes。\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 1.5\n      avg_CAR: 18.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.42\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.0\n      spatial_bowl_sdf_CAR: 18\n      sdf_delta_CAR_over_baseline: 5.0\n      task0_TSR: 0\n      task0_CAR: 22\n      task1_TSR: 6\n      task1_CAR: 12\n      task2_TSR: 0\n      task2_CAR: 20\n      task3_TSR: 0\n      task3_CAR: 18\n      n_episodes: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设 spatial_bowl SDF CAR 提升 5-12pp，效果存在但弱于 object_pudding。\n      逻辑：(1) spatial_bowl baseline CAR=13% (eval_pi05_safelibero_spatial_v11)，远低于\n      object_pudding 的 28%——scene 本身碰撞更多因为 bowl 需要在多个障碍物间抓取，arm-body\n      碰撞占主导而 EE-only SDF 对此无能为力（Claim 3）。(2) SDF 在 spatial_bowl 的增量\n      预计约 +5pp（CAR 从 13% 到 ~18%），因为 EE-only SDF gradient 能部分帮助 EE 避障\n      但 arm-body 碰撞依然发生。(3) TSR 同样大幅下降（baseline 57.5% → ~1.5%），tradeoff\n      pattern 与 object_pudding 一致但 CAR 绝对值低得多。(4) EE displacement ~0.42m\n      确认 real avoidance（非 fake safety），但效果有限。fake_safe_rate=0% 与 object_pudding\n      一致。为什么 SDF 效果弱：spatial_bowl 中障碍物（plate, ramekin, stove）位置使得\n      EE 避开它们时 arm 反而更容易扫过其他障碍物——这正是 EE-only SDF 的结构性限制。\n      median 档下 scenes_with_sdf_effect 为 1-2，spatial_bowl 算 \"weak effect\" 的第 2 个。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Scene SDF Effect Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"Baseline CAR\", \"SDF CAR\", \"Delta\", \"Baseline TSR\", \"SDF TSR\", \"Dominant Collision Type\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"27%\", \"52.5%\", \"+25.5pp\", \"73%\", \"7%\", \"EE-obstacle\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"13%\", \"~18%\", \"~+5pp\", \"57.5%\", \"~1.5%\", \"arm-body\"]\n      - name: \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Notes\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pick_bowl_between_plate_ramekin\", \"0%\", \"22%\", \"0.45\", \"arm sweeps plate despite EE avoidance\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_ramekin\", \"6%\", \"12%\", \"0.38\", \"ramekin under bowl, unavoidable arm contact\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_stove\", \"0%\", \"20%\", \"0.44\", \"stove edges cause arm-body collision\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_cabinet\", \"0%\", \"18%\", \"0.40\", \"cabinet geometry blocks safe arm paths\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: object_pudding vs spatial_bowl SDF delta, 展示 cross-scene effect attenuation\"\n      - \"Collision heatmap: EE vs arm-body collision locations, 展示 spatial_bowl 中 arm-body dominance\"\n    analysis: >\n      spatial_bowl SDF 效果弱（+5pp vs object_pudding +25pp）确认 EE-only SDF 的结构性限制——\n      当碰撞主要发生在 arm body 时，EE-level geometric supervision 效果有限。这同时支持\n      Claim 3 (EE-only limitation) 和弱化 Claim 4 的 generalization。论文措辞：\"SDF effect\n      attenuates in scenes where arm-body collisions dominate, confirming the structural \n      limitation of end-effector-only geometric supervision.\" 对 R1 泛化性 concern：\n      2 scenes 有 SDF 效果（1 strong + 1 weak）比 1 scene 好，但效果差异大需要解释。\n      mechanistic argument（EE-only vs full-body SDF）提供了解释框架。scenes_with_sdf_effect=2\n      落在 median 档预期范围内。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 bracket training (1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      高 lambda (0.1) 单 seed 训练，构建 4-point lambda 曲线 (0/LoRA, 0.005, 0.01, 0.1)。\n    expected_results:\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      best_loss: 0.0185\n      final_loss: 0.0220\n      sdf_loss_final: 0.0012\n      action_loss_final: 0.0175\n      wall_time_hours: 34\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      λ=0.1 是 λ=0.01 的 10x，SDF loss 权重显著增加。预计 total loss 更高因为 SDF loss\n      占比更大，action loss 被进一步牺牲。训练应该稳定（λ=0.01 已验证稳定），但 action\n      prediction quality 会进一步下降。best_loss 预计 ~0.0185（vs λ=0.01 的 ~0.009，\n      λ=0.005 的 ~0.008）——大部分增量来自 SDF loss 贡献。此实验是 P1 因为主要用于\n      构建曲线，不是论文核心数据。如果 LoRA baseline CAR ≈ SDF CAR 则取消（但 median\n      档下 LoRA CAR ~38% < SDF 52.5% 所以会继续）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练数据用于 eval (plan_010)。loss 曲线本身可作为 supplementary 展示 lambda 对\n      action loss 的 dose-dependent degradation。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      λ=0.1 训练完成后 eval，验证 lambda 递增是否 monotonic 提升 CAR。200 episodes。\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 1.5\n      avg_CAR: 58.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.55\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.0\n      task0_TSR: 0\n      task0_CAR: 70\n      task1_TSR: 6\n      task1_CAR: 50\n      task2_TSR: 0\n      task2_CAR: 92\n      task3_TSR: 0\n      task3_CAR: 20\n      n_episodes: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      λ=0.1 进一步增强 SDF supervision 权重，预计 CAR 继续 monotonic 上升但边际递减。\n      从 λ=0.005 (CAR ~52.5%) 到 λ=0.01 (CAR ~53%)，增量已经很小（~0.5pp）。λ=0.1\n      预计再增 ~5pp 到 ~58%，因为更强的 geometric supervision 让 EE 更积极避障，但\n      EE-only 的结构性上限限制了进一步提升。TSR 进一步下降到 ~1.5%（接近零），因为极强的\n      SDF loss 几乎完全压制了 task execution。这构成 4-point 曲线：λ=0 (LoRA, CAR 38%,\n      TSR 36.5%) → λ=0.005 (CAR 52.5%, TSR 7%) → λ=0.01 (CAR 53%, TSR 7%) →\n      λ=0.1 (CAR 58%, TSR 1.5%)。曲线展示 CAR 的 diminishing returns + TSR 的 floor effect。\n      这支持 \"naive lambda scaling 不是 solution\" 的叙事，为 future work（adaptive lambda,\n      curriculum）提供 motivation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"4-Point Lambda Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Lambda\", \"Source\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (LoRA only)\", \"plan_003\", \"36.5%\", \"38%\", \"0.31\", \"16.5%\"]\n          - [\"0.005\", \"3-seed avg\", \"7%\", \"52.5%\", \"0.50\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"0.01\", \"3-seed avg\", \"7%\", \"53%\", \"0.50\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"plan_010\", \"1.5%\", \"~58%\", \"~0.55\", \"0%\"]\n      - name: \"Lambda Curve Marginal Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Lambda Step\", \"Delta CAR\", \"Delta TSR\", \"CAR per TSR pp Lost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 → 0.005\", \"+14.5pp\", \"-29.5pp\", \"0.49\"]\n          - [\"0.005 → 0.01\", \"+0.5pp\", \"~0pp\", \"∞\"]\n          - [\"0.01 → 0.1\", \"+5pp\", \"-5.5pp\", \"0.91\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5 (paper figure): dual-y-axis plot, x=log(lambda), y1=CAR (ascending, saturating), y2=TSR (descending, floor at ~0%), with LoRA baseline as λ=0 anchor. Key insight: CAR saturates while TSR collapses\"\n    analysis: >\n      4-point lambda 曲线是 median 档的 key deliverable。它展示：(1) SDF 的 dose-dependent\n      safety effect 存在但 saturating；(2) TSR 的 catastrophic decline 在 λ=0.005 已经发生，\n      更高 lambda 只是 marginal 恶化；(3) 最优 tradeoff 点（如果存在）在 λ < 0.005 区间，\n      需要 finer-grained search（future work）。R3 \"no solution\" 应对：曲线本身就是\n      methodological contribution——展示了 lambda 空间的 landscape，为后续优化提供 guidance。\n      R5 \"tradeoff too extreme\" 应对：曲线证明 tradeoff 是 dose-dependent 的，暗示\n      adaptive/curriculum 策略可能找到更好的 operating point。\n\n  - name: \"Claim 1 full A1 re-eval decision\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      基于 plan_001 的 50ep 结果，决定是否需要 800ep full re-eval with EE displacement。\n    expected_results:\n      decision: \"no_full_reeval_needed\"\n      rationale: \"50ep EE displacement confirms ≈0, consistent with 800ep obstacle displacement data\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 plan_001 的 50ep sanity check 应确认 EE displacement ≈ 0（与已有 800ep\n      obstacle displacement 数据一致）。既然两个独立 displacement 指标都确认 action collapse，\n      就不需要花 10 GPU-hours 做 800ep full re-eval——50ep 已足够作为 \"术语验证\" 证据。\n      论文中报告 \"800ep obstacle displacement + 50ep EE displacement 双重确认\" 即可。\n      只有当 50ep 出现意外结果（如 EE displacement 意外高）才需要 full re-eval，但在\n      median 档下这不会发生。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      这是一个 decision point 而非独立实验。主要价值是节省 GPU 资源。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20955,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20955},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a636303f-80b8-415b-ba2d-90f2940539ca","uuid":"41541470-f0d9-4fc0-a4f8-6115f6da39ef"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":203845,"duration_api_ms":205318,"num_turns":1,"result":"我先检查已有的实验数据和计划，确保预测与已确认结果一致。\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Median 档叙事：SDF 是有效的 geometric safety probe，但 LoRA 本身贡献了非小部分 CAR 提升（~35-40%），\n  SDF 增量约 +12-17pp。Phase 2 λ=0 结果为 informative negative——TSR 恢复但 CAR 回落，证明 safety\n  encoding 不持久，需持续 supervision。OpenVLA 验证 fake safety 存在但信号弱于 Pi0。spatial_bowl\n  SDF 效果存在但弱于 object_pudding。论文定位 diagnostic paper，SDF 作为 probe 而非 solution。\n  Acceptance 估算 50-60%。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"A1 EE displacement re-eval (50 episodes)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      用修复后 eval 脚本重跑 A1 (Pi0+LoRA+SDF) model 在 object_pudding 上 50 episodes，\n      提取真实 EE displacement 以定量确认 Claim 1 fake safety。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes: 50\n      avg_TSR: 0\n      avg_CAR: 91.0\n      avg_ee_displacement_m: 0.0021\n      avg_obstacle_displacement_mm: 0.003\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.995\n      real_safe_count: 0\n      episodes_with_ee_disp_gt_0p1m: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 800ep rerun (eval_a1_lora_object_v11_rerun) 确认 CAR=91.5%、fake_safe_rate=99.6%、\n      obstacle displacement 中位数 ~5nm。在 median 档下，修复后脚本新增的 EE displacement 字段预计\n      同样极低（~2mm），因为 A1 模型 TSR=0% 表明 action collapse——robot 几乎不动，EE 位移自然极小。\n      这 50ep sanity check 应与 800ep 数据高度一致，确认 \"EE displacement 接近零 = fake safety\"\n      的定量证据链。不会出现意外高 EE displacement，因为 action collapse 是结构性的。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"A1 EE Displacement Sanity Check (50ep)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"800ep Rerun\", \"50ep Re-eval\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"TSR\", \"0%\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"CAR\", \"91.5%\", \"~91%\"]\n          - [\"Fake Safe Rate\", \"99.6%\", \"~99.5%\"]\n          - [\"Avg Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"0.003\", \"~0.003\"]\n          - [\"Avg EE Disp (m)\", \"N/A (old script)\", \"~0.002\"]\n          - [\"Episodes EE>0.1m\", \"N/A\", \"0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: per-episode EE displacement 分布, 预期全部集中在 <5mm, 与 800ep obstacle displacement 分布形态一致\"\n    analysis: >\n      确认 A1 的 fake safety 同时表现为 obstacle displacement ≈0 和 EE displacement ≈0。\n      这两个独立指标双重验证 action collapse。50ep 与 800ep 一致则不需要 full re-eval (plan_011 取消)。\n      论文中可同时报告两种 displacement 指标增强 Claim 1 说服力。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA zero-shot SafeLIBERO eval (200 episodes)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      Base OpenVLA-7B 在 object_pudding 4 tasks 零样本 eval，200 episodes，\n      验证 fake safety 或 geometric path safety 在第三 model family 上的表现。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes: 200\n      avg_TSR: 8.0\n      avg_CAR: 72.0\n      avg_obstacle_displacement_mm: 12.0\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.70\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 82\n      task1_TSR: 18\n      task1_CAR: 52\n      task2_TSR: 6\n      task2_CAR: 80\n      task3_TSR: 4\n      task3_CAR: 74\n      ee_displacement_m: 0.08\n      model_families_showing_fake_safety: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设：OpenVLA eval 成功但 fake safety 信号弱于 Pi0。OpenVLA-7B 是更小的\n      模型（7B vs Pi0 ~3B action head），zero-shot 在 SafeLIBERO 上 TSR 预计很低（~5-10%），\n      因为它没有在该 benchmark 上微调。低 TSR 意味着大量 episode 中 robot 运动有限但非完全\n      collapse（OpenVLA 的 action space 与 Pi0 不同，倾向于产生小但非零的动作）。因此 CAR 会\n      较高（~72%）但 fake_safe_rate 约 70%——低于 Pi0 的 99.6% 因为 OpenVLA 不会完全 freeze，\n      会有一些小幅运动导致 obstacle displacement 偶尔超过 0.1mm 阈值。这给出 \"fake safety\n      exists in OpenVLA but weaker\" 的 median 结论：第三 model family 确认了现象存在，\n      但强度不一致，需在论文中 qualify。部分 task（如 chocolate_pudding 有更大障碍物）CAR\n      会更低因为 OpenVLA 即使小运动也会碰到。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"OpenVLA Zero-Shot Fake Safety Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Fake Safe Rate\", \"Avg Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"Avg EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0 A1 (LoRA+SDF)\", \"0%\", \"91.5%\", \"99.6%\", \"0.003\", \"~0.002\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 Baseline\", \"73%\", \"28%\", \"98.2% (of safe eps)\", \"150.8\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA-7B Zero-Shot\", \"~8%\", \"~72%\", \"~70%\", \"~12\", \"~0.08\"]\n      - name: \"OpenVLA Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"Notes\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"4%\", \"82%\", \"~5\", \"low motion, mostly fake safe\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"18%\", \"52%\", \"~28\", \"larger obstacle, more real collisions\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"6%\", \"80%\", \"~8\", \"moderate fake safety\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"4%\", \"74%\", \"~10\", \"mixed fake/geometric safety\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: 3 model families on TSR vs CAR plane, 标注 fake_safe_rate 作为 marker size, 展示 cross-model fake safety pattern\"\n      - \"Bar chart: fake_safe_rate comparison across Pi0 A1 / Pi0.5 baseline / OpenVLA, 展示现象普遍性但强度差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA 确认 fake safety 存在于第三 model family，使 Claim 1 从 \"Pi0-specific\" 升级为\n      \"cross-model phenomenon\"。但信号弱于 Pi0（70% vs 99.6%），论文需 qualify：fake safety\n      的严重程度与 model capability 和 action space 结构相关。Pi0 action collapse 最极端，\n      OpenVLA 有部分运动但仍大量 fake safe。Pi0.5 的 fake safe 集中在 safe episodes 中\n      （task capability 高所以 safe episodes 少）。三个 model family 共同支持 \"CAR metric is\n      systematically contaminated\" 但机制略有不同。R1 泛化性 concern 从 \"2 models\" 升级到\n      \"3 models\"，acceptance 估算从 ~40% 提升到 ~55%。可能需要 debug OpenVLA 的 action\n      decoding 确保 eval 正确运行（median 档预期部分 debug 时间）。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds, 30K checkpoint)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      LoRA baseline (Pi0.5 + LoRA, 无 SDF) 训练完成后在 object_pudding 200ep eval，\n      2 seeds 取均值，确定 LoRA-only CAR 从而决定 SDF 归因强度。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_TSR: 38.0\n      seed0_CAR: 37.0\n      seed0_ee_disp: 0.32\n      seed0_fake_safe_rate: 0.15\n      seed1_TSR: 35.0\n      seed1_CAR: 39.0\n      seed1_ee_disp: 0.29\n      seed1_fake_safe_rate: 0.18\n      avg_TSR: 36.5\n      avg_CAR: 38.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.305\n      avg_fake_safe_rate: 0.165\n      sdf_delta_CAR: 14.5\n      n_episodes_per_seed: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设 LoRA-only CAR 在 35-42% 范围。逻辑：Pi0.5 baseline（无 LoRA 无 SDF）\n      CAR=26.8%。LoRA 微调增加模型在 SafeLIBERO 上的 capacity，但没有 geometric supervision\n      引导避障。LoRA 可能通过学到 task-specific 运动模式间接提升 CAR——比如学会更高效的路径\n      从而减少与障碍物接触的机会。但这不是 intentional avoidance。预计 TSR ~36.5%（低于\n      baseline 73% 因为 LoRA 在 SafeLIBERO 上的 fine-tuning 可能引入 distribution shift，\n      但高于 SDF 版本的 5-9% 因为没有 SDF loss 干扰 task execution）。CAR ~38% 意味着\n      SDF 增量 = 52.5% (avg SDF CAR) - 38% = +14.5pp。这落在 median 档的 10-18pp 范围内。\n      LoRA 本身提供 +11pp over baseline（38% - 27%），SDF 额外提供 +14.5pp。叙事变为\n      \"LoRA helps, SDF adds major benefit\"——第二行归因表。fake_safe_rate 约 16% 因为部分\n      episode 中 LoRA 模型运动受限但非完全 collapse。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"LoRA Attribution Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe Rate\", \"Delta CAR vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 Baseline (no FT)\", \"73%\", \"27%\", \"0.15\", \"98.2%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA only\", \"~36.5%\", \"~38%\", \"~0.31\", \"~16.5%\", \"+11pp\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.005)\", \"5.5-9.5%\", \"50-55%\", \"~0.50\", \"0%\", \"+25pp\"]\n      - name: \"SDF vs LoRA Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Component\", \"CAR Contribution\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline geometric path\", \"27%\", \"Inherent path safety of capable model\"]\n          - [\"LoRA capacity effect\", \"+11pp → 38%\", \"Task-specific motion patterns reduce incidental contact\"]\n          - [\"SDF geometric supervision\", \"+14.5pp → 52.5%\", \"Intentional collision avoidance from SDF gradient\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Lambda-CAR/TSR curve (Fig 5): x=lambda {0(LoRA), 0.005, 0.01}, y1=CAR, y2=TSR, 展示 dose-dependent tradeoff, LoRA baseline 作为 λ=0 anchor point\"\n    analysis: >\n      LoRA-only CAR ~38% 确认 SDF 不是唯一驱动力——LoRA 本身通过 capacity 增加间接提升了\n      CAR。但 SDF 增量 +14.5pp 仍然显著且方向一致（3 seeds 确认）。Claim 4 措辞需调整为\n      \"SDF provides additive safety benefit beyond LoRA capacity — geometric supervision\n      amplifies rather than solely drives collision avoidance.\" Lambda 曲线现在有 3 个点\n      (0/0.005/0.01)，呈现 monotonic CAR 增加 + TSR 下降的 dose-dependent pattern。\n      如果后续有 λ=0.1 数据则曲线更完整。fake_safe_rate 从 baseline 98.2% → LoRA 16.5% →\n      SDF 0% 的递减也是有价值的发现：LoRA 微调本身就大幅减少了 fake safety（因为 TSR 下降\n      意味着 model 不再是 baseline 的 \"高能力低碰撞\" 模式），SDF 则完全消除 fake safety。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline training completion (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      Pi0.5 + LoRA only (无 SDF loss) 训练到 30K steps, 2 seeds。已在运行中。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_steps_completed: 30000\n      seed0_best_loss: 0.0068\n      seed0_final_loss: 0.0085\n      seed1_steps_completed: 30000\n      seed1_best_loss: 0.0072\n      seed1_final_loss: 0.0090\n      wall_time_hours_per_seed: 16\n    result_rationale: >\n      LoRA-only 训练 loss 预计低于 A1 (LoRA+SDF) 因为没有 SDF auxiliary loss 的干扰。\n      已有 A1 数据：s0_l005 best_loss=0.00786, s1_l005 best_loss=0.01143, s2_l005 \n      best_loss=0.00874。LoRA-only 去掉 SDF loss 后 action loss 应更低（best ~0.007），\n      因为全部 gradient capacity 用于 action prediction。训练应正常完成，无 collapse 风险\n      （LoRA-only 是标准 fine-tuning，比 SDF auxiliary 训练更稳定）。当前 step 26000/30000,\n      预计 ~3.5h 完成。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练本身是 dependency，关键在 eval 结果。loss 曲线可作为 supplementary 展示\n      SDF loss 对 action loss 的干扰程度。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 λ=0 ablation training (seed2, from 10K SDF checkpoint)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      从 Pi0.5+A1 s2 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume 训练 with λ=0 (关闭 SDF loss)，\n      训练到 30K，验证 safety encoding 是否在去除 SDF 后保留。\n    expected_results:\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      best_action_loss: 0.0075\n      final_action_loss: 0.0092\n      training_stable: true\n      wall_time_hours: 16\n      sdf_loss_at_resume: 0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 SDF-trained checkpoint resume with λ=0 时，action loss 预计初始偏高（因为 SDF\n      训练 10K 步偏离了 pure action prediction 的 optimum），然后逐步恢复。训练本身应该\n      稳定——只是标准 LoRA fine-tuning 从一个非标准初始化点开始。最终 action loss 应\n      接近 LoRA-only 水平（~0.008）但可能略高因为 10K 步的 SDF 训练改变了 representation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练结果本身不直接回答科学问题——关键是 eval (plan_006)。但 loss 曲线可以展示\n      action loss 从 SDF-perturbed state 恢复的动态，作为 \"safety encoding 被覆盖\" \n      的间接证据。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 λ=0 eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Phase 2 训练完成后 eval (200 episodes)，提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement，\n      判断 safety encoding 是否保留。\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 42.0\n      avg_CAR: 32.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.28\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.12\n      task0_TSR: 30\n      task0_CAR: 38\n      task1_TSR: 68\n      task1_CAR: 26\n      task2_TSR: 20\n      task2_CAR: 52\n      task3_TSR: 50\n      task3_CAR: 12\n      n_episodes: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设：TSR 恢复到 30-50% 但 CAR 回落至 30-35%。逻辑链：(1) 关闭 SDF loss\n      后模型恢复 task execution 能力（TSR 从 5-9% 回到 ~42%，不完全恢复到 baseline 73%\n      因为 10K 步 SDF 训练改变了 representation 且只有 20K 步恢复时间）；(2) CAR 回落到 ~32%\n      接近 LoRA-only 水平（~38%）甚至略低，说明 SDF 诱导的 safety encoding 没有被 \"烙印\"\n      到 representation 中——一旦 loss signal 消失，model 迅速遗忘。这是 informative negative：\n      safety 需要 continuous supervision，10K 步的 geometric training 不足以产生持久的\n      behavioral change。TSR 42% < baseline 73% 说明 SDF 训练 phase 造成了部分不可逆的\n      capability 损失（task performance 未完全恢复），但不是 catastrophic（仍有合理的 task\n      completion）。CAR 32% 接近 baseline 27% + LoRA effect，意味着 SDF 的 safety 增量\n      完全消失。fake_safe_rate ~12% 类似 LoRA-only 水平。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Phase 2 λ=0 Ablation Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 Baseline\", \"73%\", \"27%\", \"0.15\", \"98.2%\"]\n          - [\"SDF λ=0.005 (continuous)\", \"5.5-9.5%\", \"50-55%\", \"0.50\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"Phase 2 λ=0 (from 10K SDF)\", \"~42%\", \"~32%\", \"~0.28\", \"~12%\"]\n          - [\"LoRA only (no SDF ever)\", \"~36.5%\", \"~38%\", \"~0.31\", \"~16.5%\"]\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Interpretation Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Outcome\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"Interpretation\", \"Paper Impact\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Observed (median)\", \"42%\", \"32%\", \"Safety encoding not persistent\", \"Informative negative\"]\n          - [\"Upgrade threshold\", \">=40%\", \">=40%\", \"Two-phase strategy works\", \"Solution paper\"]\n          - [\"Strong negative\", \"<20%\", \"any\", \"SDF causes irreversible damage\", \"Supports extreme tradeoff\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training dynamics plot: action loss over steps 10K-30K for Phase 2 vs LoRA-only vs SDF-continuous, showing recovery trajectory\"\n      - \"TSR-CAR scatter: Phase 2 point added to existing scatter, showing it lands between LoRA-only and baseline\"\n    analysis: >\n      Phase 2 结果为 informative negative：TSR 恢复（42%）证明 SDF 训练没有 permanently\n      破坏 task capability，但 CAR 回落到 ~32% 证明 safety encoding 不持久。这排除了\n      \"two-phase training strategy\" 作为 technical contribution（不满足 TSR≥40% + CAR≥40%\n      双门槛）。论文写入方式：\"Removing SDF supervision recovers task performance (TSR: 9%→42%)\n      but safety gains are lost (CAR: 52%→32%), indicating that SDF-induced collision avoidance\n      requires continuous geometric supervision rather than being encoded as a persistent\n      behavioral prior.\" 这支持 diagnostic paper 定位——问题可解但 naive 方法不持久。\n      R3 \"no solution\" concern 通过此 negative result + Phase 2/lambda tuning 作为\n      future work 来应对。CAR 32% 略低于 LoRA-only 38%（差 6pp）可能在 noise 范围内，\n      也可能说明 SDF 训练 phase 对 representation 的 perturbation 稍微损害了 LoRA \n      已学到的 incidental safety patterns。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 训练 (seed0, λ=0.005)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (A1) 在 spatial_bowl scene 训练 30K steps，\n      验证 SDF 效果是否跨 scene 泛化。\n    expected_results:\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      best_loss: 0.0125\n      final_loss: 0.0155\n      wall_time_hours: 34\n      sdf_loss_final: 0.0035\n    result_rationale: >\n      spatial_bowl 是更难的 scene（障碍物布局不同，碰撞部位更多 arm-body 而非 EE）。\n      SDF training loss 预计略高于 object_pudding（s0_l005 best=0.00786）因为 scene\n      complexity 增加了 action prediction 难度。训练本身应正常完成（已确认 A1 训练在\n      object_pudding 上 3 seeds 稳定）。当前 11329/30000 步，~24h 剩余。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练是 dependency，关键在 eval (plan_008)。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval，验证跨场景 CAR/TSR pattern。200 episodes。\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 1.5\n      avg_CAR: 18.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.42\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.0\n      spatial_bowl_sdf_CAR: 18\n      sdf_delta_CAR_over_baseline: 5.0\n      task0_TSR: 0\n      task0_CAR: 22\n      task1_TSR: 6\n      task1_CAR: 12\n      task2_TSR: 0\n      task2_CAR: 20\n      task3_TSR: 0\n      task3_CAR: 18\n      n_episodes: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档假设 spatial_bowl SDF CAR 提升 5-12pp，效果存在但弱于 object_pudding。\n      逻辑：(1) spatial_bowl baseline CAR=13% (eval_pi05_safelibero_spatial_v11)，远低于\n      object_pudding 的 28%——scene 本身碰撞更多因为 bowl 需要在多个障碍物间抓取，arm-body\n      碰撞占主导而 EE-only SDF 对此无能为力（Claim 3）。(2) SDF 在 spatial_bowl 的增量\n      预计约 +5pp（CAR 从 13% 到 ~18%），因为 EE-only SDF gradient 能部分帮助 EE 避障\n      但 arm-body 碰撞依然发生。(3) TSR 同样大幅下降（baseline 57.5% → ~1.5%），tradeoff\n      pattern 与 object_pudding 一致但 CAR 绝对值低得多。(4) EE displacement ~0.42m\n      确认 real avoidance（非 fake safety），但效果有限。fake_safe_rate=0% 与 object_pudding\n      一致。为什么 SDF 效果弱：spatial_bowl 中障碍物（plate, ramekin, stove）位置使得\n      EE 避开它们时 arm 反而更容易扫过其他障碍物——这正是 EE-only SDF 的结构性限制。\n      median 档下 scenes_with_sdf_effect 为 1-2，spatial_bowl 算 \"weak effect\" 的第 2 个。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Scene SDF Effect Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"Baseline CAR\", \"SDF CAR\", \"Delta\", \"Baseline TSR\", \"SDF TSR\", \"Dominant Collision Type\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"27%\", \"52.5%\", \"+25.5pp\", \"73%\", \"7%\", \"EE-obstacle\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"13%\", \"~18%\", \"~+5pp\", \"57.5%\", \"~1.5%\", \"arm-body\"]\n      - name: \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Notes\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pick_bowl_between_plate_ramekin\", \"0%\", \"22%\", \"0.45\", \"arm sweeps plate despite EE avoidance\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_ramekin\", \"6%\", \"12%\", \"0.38\", \"ramekin under bowl, unavoidable arm contact\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_stove\", \"0%\", \"20%\", \"0.44\", \"stove edges cause arm-body collision\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_cabinet\", \"0%\", \"18%\", \"0.40\", \"cabinet geometry blocks safe arm paths\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: object_pudding vs spatial_bowl SDF delta, 展示 cross-scene effect attenuation\"\n      - \"Collision heatmap: EE vs arm-body collision locations, 展示 spatial_bowl 中 arm-body dominance\"\n    analysis: >\n      spatial_bowl SDF 效果弱（+5pp vs object_pudding +25pp）确认 EE-only SDF 的结构性限制——\n      当碰撞主要发生在 arm body 时，EE-level geometric supervision 效果有限。这同时支持\n      Claim 3 (EE-only limitation) 和弱化 Claim 4 的 generalization。论文措辞：\"SDF effect\n      attenuates in scenes where arm-body collisions dominate, confirming the structural \n      limitation of end-effector-only geometric supervision.\" 对 R1 泛化性 concern：\n      2 scenes 有 SDF 效果（1 strong + 1 weak）比 1 scene 好，但效果差异大需要解释。\n      mechanistic argument（EE-only vs full-body SDF）提供了解释框架。scenes_with_sdf_effect=2\n      落在 median 档预期范围内。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 bracket training (1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      高 lambda (0.1) 单 seed 训练，构建 4-point lambda 曲线 (0/LoRA, 0.005, 0.01, 0.1)。\n    expected_results:\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      best_loss: 0.0185\n      final_loss: 0.0220\n      sdf_loss_final: 0.0012\n      action_loss_final: 0.0175\n      wall_time_hours: 34\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      λ=0.1 是 λ=0.01 的 10x，SDF loss 权重显著增加。预计 total loss 更高因为 SDF loss\n      占比更大，action loss 被进一步牺牲。训练应该稳定（λ=0.01 已验证稳定），但 action\n      prediction quality 会进一步下降。best_loss 预计 ~0.0185（vs λ=0.01 的 ~0.009，\n      λ=0.005 的 ~0.008）——大部分增量来自 SDF loss 贡献。此实验是 P1 因为主要用于\n      构建曲线，不是论文核心数据。如果 LoRA baseline CAR ≈ SDF CAR 则取消（但 median\n      档下 LoRA CAR ~38% < SDF 52.5% 所以会继续）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练数据用于 eval (plan_010)。loss 曲线本身可作为 supplementary 展示 lambda 对\n      action loss 的 dose-dependent degradation。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      λ=0.1 训练完成后 eval，验证 lambda 递增是否 monotonic 提升 CAR。200 episodes。\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 1.5\n      avg_CAR: 58.0\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.55\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.0\n      task0_TSR: 0\n      task0_CAR: 70\n      task1_TSR: 6\n      task1_CAR: 50\n      task2_TSR: 0\n      task2_CAR: 92\n      task3_TSR: 0\n      task3_CAR: 20\n      n_episodes: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      λ=0.1 进一步增强 SDF supervision 权重，预计 CAR 继续 monotonic 上升但边际递减。\n      从 λ=0.005 (CAR ~52.5%) 到 λ=0.01 (CAR ~53%)，增量已经很小（~0.5pp）。λ=0.1\n      预计再增 ~5pp 到 ~58%，因为更强的 geometric supervision 让 EE 更积极避障，但\n      EE-only 的结构性上限限制了进一步提升。TSR 进一步下降到 ~1.5%（接近零），因为极强的\n      SDF loss 几乎完全压制了 task execution。这构成 4-point 曲线：λ=0 (LoRA, CAR 38%,\n      TSR 36.5%) → λ=0.005 (CAR 52.5%, TSR 7%) → λ=0.01 (CAR 53%, TSR 7%) →\n      λ=0.1 (CAR 58%, TSR 1.5%)。曲线展示 CAR 的 diminishing returns + TSR 的 floor effect。\n      这支持 \"naive lambda scaling 不是 solution\" 的叙事，为 future work（adaptive lambda,\n      curriculum）提供 motivation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"4-Point Lambda Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Lambda\", \"Source\", \"TSR\", \"CAR\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (LoRA only)\", \"plan_003\", \"36.5%\", \"38%\", \"0.31\", \"16.5%\"]\n          - [\"0.005\", \"3-seed avg\", \"7%\", \"52.5%\", \"0.50\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"0.01\", \"3-seed avg\", \"7%\", \"53%\", \"0.50\", \"0%\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"plan_010\", \"1.5%\", \"~58%\", \"~0.55\", \"0%\"]\n      - name: \"Lambda Curve Marginal Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Lambda Step\", \"Delta CAR\", \"Delta TSR\", \"CAR per TSR pp Lost\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 → 0.005\", \"+14.5pp\", \"-29.5pp\", \"0.49\"]\n          - [\"0.005 → 0.01\", \"+0.5pp\", \"~0pp\", \"∞\"]\n          - [\"0.01 → 0.1\", \"+5pp\", \"-5.5pp\", \"0.91\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5 (paper figure): dual-y-axis plot, x=log(lambda), y1=CAR (ascending, saturating), y2=TSR (descending, floor at ~0%), with LoRA baseline as λ=0 anchor. Key insight: CAR saturates while TSR collapses\"\n    analysis: >\n      4-point lambda 曲线是 median 档的 key deliverable。它展示：(1) SDF 的 dose-dependent\n      safety effect 存在但 saturating；(2) TSR 的 catastrophic decline 在 λ=0.005 已经发生，\n      更高 lambda 只是 marginal 恶化；(3) 最优 tradeoff 点（如果存在）在 λ < 0.005 区间，\n      需要 finer-grained search（future work）。R3 \"no solution\" 应对：曲线本身就是\n      methodological contribution——展示了 lambda 空间的 landscape，为后续优化提供 guidance。\n      R5 \"tradeoff too extreme\" 应对：曲线证明 tradeoff 是 dose-dependent 的，暗示\n      adaptive/curriculum 策略可能找到更好的 operating point。\n\n  - name: \"Claim 1 full A1 re-eval decision\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      基于 plan_001 的 50ep 结果，决定是否需要 800ep full re-eval with EE displacement。\n    expected_results:\n      decision: \"no_full_reeval_needed\"\n      rationale: \"50ep EE displacement confirms ≈0, consistent with 800ep obstacle displacement data\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 plan_001 的 50ep sanity check 应确认 EE displacement ≈ 0（与已有 800ep\n      obstacle displacement 数据一致）。既然两个独立 displacement 指标都确认 action collapse，\n      就不需要花 10 GPU-hours 做 800ep full re-eval——50ep 已足够作为 \"术语验证\" 证据。\n      论文中报告 \"800ep obstacle displacement + 50ep EE displacement 双重确认\" 即可。\n      只有当 50ep 出现意外结果（如 EE displacement 意外高）才需要 full re-eval，但在\n      median 档下这不会发生。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      这是一个 decision point 而非独立实验。主要价值是节省 GPU 资源。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a636303f-80b8-415b-ba2d-90f2940539ca","total_cost_usd":0.40068625,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20955,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":9935,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20955,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9935,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20955},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":15509,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.015609,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":9935,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":20955,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.38507725000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0481596b-83d0-41cb-a566-d76129427347"}
